### Claude Code / local tooling (never commit — may contain secrets) ###
# `**/` matters: the harness lives in BOTH `.claude/` (repo root) and `docs/ai-agent/.claude/`
# (the shippable bundle). A root-anchored `.claude/settings.local.json` misses the bundle copy,
# which until now was covered only by a machine-global ~/.config/git/ignore — protection that
# does not survive a fresh clone on another machine. Keep these repo-local and path-agnostic.
.mcp.json
**/.claude/settings.local.json
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
**/.claude/**/.fetched-*

# Machine-local config that was parked inside the SHIPPED bundle and has been moved out of it.
# The rules above are anchored to `.claude/`, so a file that leaves that directory leaves their
# cover with it — this whole directory is ignored instead, because what lives in it is exactly the
# kind of thing that must never be committed: one developer's allow-list, absolute paths into
# another repository, and DEV database credentials.
.agent-local/

### Env files (never commit — secrets) ###
# `.env*` is the catch-all and MUST stay first: the earlier rules `.env` / `*.env` / `.env.*` all
# require the name to END with `.env` or to have a DOT after `.env`, so a suffix spelled with an
# underscore (`.env_prodcat`, `.env_designer`) matched none of them and three files with live DEV
# Postgres credentials reached origin/master. Do not narrow this pattern again.
.env*
*.env

### stand-test KB ingestion — verbatim source stays LOCAL (never commit) ###
# The whole _source/ tree (raw binaries, converter output normalized.md, extracted media/*.emf)
# holds verbatim, un-redacted document content that may carry live hosts/credentials/PII.
# Only redacted, schema-valid candidate YAML is committed; the source is traced by document.hash.
docs/ai-agent/knowledge-base/candidates/**/_source/
knowledge-base/candidates/**/_source/
# Ad-hoc drop location for raw spec documents fed into ingestion — same rule: verbatim, never commit.
docs/source/
### stand-guard per-run state (never commit) ###
# The kit's hooks keep one state file per PROJECT: which artifacts a session wrote, which gates
# covered which content hash, the run journal. It is an artefact of one session in one checkout —
# committing it would make a stale gate verdict travel to everyone else, and the Stop gate would then
# hold a session over an artifact nobody in that checkout has. The bundle's own .gitignore covers the
# copy under docs/ai-agent/; this covers the root harness, where running the guard by hand leaves it.
.claude/.stand-test/
.opencode/.stand-test/
